#: ../../requirements.md:94
msgid "Orientation and Axes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:96
msgid ""
"This explains how the device handles magnetometer orientation and how to "
"configure 90° rotations around each axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:98
msgid "Axis conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:99
msgid "The RM3100 outputs three orthogonal components X, Y, Z."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:100
msgid "mag-usb treats these axes as a right‑handed coordinate system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:101
msgid ""
"Positive rotations follow the right‑hand rule (thumb points along the "
"axis of rotation; curl of fingers is direction of positive rotation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:103
msgid "Why orientation adjustments?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:104
msgid ""
"Depending on how the sensor PCB is mounted in your enclosure, its axes "
"may not align with your desired reference frame. mag-usb can rotate the "
"measured vector by multiples of 90° around the X, Y, and Z axes to align "
"with your installation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:106
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:107
msgid "Set the following keys in `config.toml` under `[mag_orientation]`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:114
msgid "Rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:115
msgid ""
"Allowed values: `-180, -90, 0, 90, 180`. Any other value is treated as "
"`0`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:116
msgid "`180` and `-180` are treated the same (flip both perpendicular axes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:117
msgid ""
"Rotations are applied in this order: rotate around X, then around Y, then"
" around Z."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:118
msgid "The rotations affect the other two components:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:119
msgid "Rotate around X → affects Y and Z."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:120
msgid "Rotate around Y → affects X and Z."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:121
msgid "Rotate around Z → affects X and Y."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:123
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:124
msgid "Let the input vector be `(X, Y, Z)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:126
msgid "Rotate +90° about X:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:127
msgid "`(X, Y, Z)` → `(X, -Z, Y)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:128
msgid "Rotate -90° about X:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:129
msgid "`(X, Y, Z)` → `(X, Z, -Y)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:130
msgid "Rotate 180° about X:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../requirements.md:131
msgid "`(X, Y, Z)` → `(X, -Y, -Z)`"
msgstr ""

